From: Prashant-thakur77 <prashant101007@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:12:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(execute): accept raw calldata on POST
 /api/execute/contract-call

Execution frameworks hand their executor an already-encoded data field.
Decode it against the body or explorer ABI into the canonical function key
and typed functionArgs, then take the existing read, simulate and write
paths so every guard keeps reading a named function. A selector the ABI
does not contain is a 400 on field data; no signature database is consulted.
